    "sensesNotes": "Darkvision 30 ft, Vibration Sense",
    "tactics": "Insect Swarms seek exposed faces, eyes, and gaps in clothing. They harry spellcasters and crew members trying to extinguish fires, then scatter when forced into open bright ground.",
    "attacksNotes": "<p>Stinging Cloud: Opposed Reflex save using Agil 4 + Melee Combat 2 against every creature sharing the swarm's space. Target loses: 6 piercing damage and gains Poisoned (Weak) for 1 minute. Target wins: 3 piercing damage. At half HP or lower, deal 3 piercing damage on a loss and 1 piercing damage on a win; Poisoned (Weak) still applies on a loss.</p>",
    "specialAbilitiesNotes": "<p>Distracting Buzz: A creature that takes full damage adds 1 to both dice on its next attack before the end of its next turn. Swarm Body: The Insect Swarm can occupy another creature's space and move through openings large enough for its constituent insects. Light Avoidance: In bright light, the Insect Swarm cannot Hide unless it has cover. Swarms: Swarms occupy a 5 × 5 ft space, halve physical damage, ignore Grappled, Restrained, Prone, and Bleeding, and resolve their ### Attacks as opposed Reflex saves. Each entry lists full damage and reduced damage once the swarm is at half HP or lower.</p>",
